{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrCvA5QaUfxpMTeh62b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build and all 106 checks pass after the cleanup. Next I'll fill the exit-interview answers in the about data with the real answers from this build, correct the online field to \"none\", and rebuild. I'll check the time first, for the session-time field."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3719,"cache_read_input_tokens":424707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3719},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"fd0632bc-84d7-48fb-9bf9-4f4443098ad9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:59:09.378Z","request_id":"req_011CghrCunFmjj1R3BBGRNeV"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrCvA5QaUfxpMTeh62b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VmRcuryt9HQFBoSvhwKWSB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"date && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/01-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"    online: 'AI Hub ghost session: not built in this demo (none)',\",\"    online: 'none (the AI Hub session client is downloaded but not wired in; no network features)',\")\nrep(\"    testing: 'Headless suites through the engine (game.advance and input taps), run with tests/run.mjs',\",\n    \"    testing: 'Headless suites through the engine (game.advance, input taps, scenes), 106 checks in tests/run.mjs; no browser run',\")\nrep(\"  testingFeedback: ['unknown'],\\n  engineFeedback: ['unknown'],\\n  promptFeedback: ['unknown'],\",\n\"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'About ten real defects surfaced: a stage transition that dropped the carried distance, a goal that re-entered its own stage, a fork that read stage definitions as built stages, a bus used before it was set, a drift exit tied to the wrong value, a curve push applied as a velocity increment, a drag that capped top speed near 170 km/h, a time-based traffic spawner that over-filled the road, and lane changes that oscillated.',\n    'Four would have broken a run outright: the stage skip, the goal re-entry, the fork crash and the bus crash on the first race. Each is now covered by a check.',\n    'Most helpful: the full-route bot runs, which play all 16 forks to their goals with real distances, and exposed the stage-skip bug at once.',\n    'Least helpful: the draw smoke test. It only proves the drawing code runs without an exception on a no-op renderer, so it says nothing about what appears on screen, and no browser or screenshot run was done.',\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'Most liked: the road module. E.Road with segments, curves, hills, place() and project() gave a working pseudo-3D road in a few hundred lines, and the kit gave a complete reference game to read.',\n    'Got stuck on: the game.go options (the fade is the third argument), the pause menu item and setting shapes, and the headless draw path, which needs a canvas stub for road.draw (E.mkCanvas) and a renderer that answers every call. Guessed the Backdrop draw signature from the kit.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the car model (acceleration calibrated to each car\\\\'s 0-100 rating, steering with the curve push, drift, slipstream, off-road), the traffic and lane logic, the driver brain, the run rules and the request rules.',\n    'Hardest part: a fork needs two roads drawn at once, and road.draw paints one road over the frame. Without a split-road renderer the fork is only signposted, and the road switches at the junction end.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. Analog triggers are read from navigator.getGamepads() in game code, and the split-road renderer, the analog input and the other planned engine changes were not made.',\n    'One change I would make: a headless renderer or canvas stub in the engine, so draw code can run in tests without a browser.',\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'Most liked: the plan is concrete. Every tuning number, every stage layout and every test suite is written down, which made the physics and the data quick to start.',\n    'Confusing: the plan was written for a different run (other model, other date, other folder names), and it asks for far more than one session can build (16 routes, 14 requests, 14 missions, 11 songs, Versus, the garden, AI Hub) with no cut list. TASK.md and the plan also disagree on the names, which made me choose TASK.md each time.',\n    'Hardest: getting the bot to hold the balance windows without a pad to tune by hand, and making a fork read as a fork without a split-road renderer.',\n    'Would change: give this run its own names and dates, state what to cut when time runs short, state the balance as a clock rule (the time per stage and the checkpoint bonus) rather than as bot windows, and say whether the bot uses the player\\\\'s physics.',\n  ],\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('about ok')\nEOF\nnode --check src/01-about.js && timeout 120 node build.mjs | tail -1 && python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d.keys()), len(d['testingFeedback']), len(d['engineFeedback']), len(d['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Fill feedback answers, rebuild, and validate the exit JSON"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3719,"cache_read_input_tokens":424707,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3719},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"84200749-44ca-4891-8123-5c352bc59048","timestamp":"2026-11-04T11:59:17.087Z","request_id":"req_011CghrCunFmjj1R3BBGRNeV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VmRcuryt9HQFBoSvhwKWSB":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-043153__xe1b7e1/work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153 && date && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/01-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"    online: 'AI Hub ghost session: not built in this demo (none)',\",\"    online: 'none (the AI Hub session client is downloaded but not wired in; no network features)',\")\nrep(\"    testing: 'Headless suites through the engine (game.advance and input taps), run with tests/run.mjs',\",\n    \"    testing: 'Headless suites through the engine (game.advance, input taps, scenes), 106 checks in tests/run.mjs; no browser run',\")\nrep(\"  testingFeedback: ['unknown'],\\n  engineFeedback: ['unknown'],\\n  promptFeedback: ['unknown'],\",\n\"\"\"  testingFeedback: [\n    'About ten real defects surfaced: a stage transition that dropped the carried distance, a goal that re-entered its own stage, a fork that read stage definitions as built stages, a bus used before it was set, a drift exit tied to the wrong value, a curve push applied as a velocity increment, a drag that capped top speed near 170 km/h, a time-based traffic spawner that over-filled the road, and lane changes that oscillated.',\n    'Four would have broken a run outright: the stage skip, the goal re-entry, the fork crash and the bus crash on the first race. Each is now covered by a check.',\n    'Most helpful: the full-route bot runs, which play all 16 forks to their goals with real distances, and exposed the stage-skip bug at once.',\n    'Least helpful: the draw smoke test. It only proves the drawing code runs without an exception on a no-op renderer, so it says nothing about what appears on screen, and no browser or screenshot run was done.',\n  ],\n  engineFeedback: [\n    'Most liked: the road module. E.Road with segments, curves, hills, place() and project() gave a working pseudo-3D road in a few hundred lines, and the kit gave a complete reference game to read.',\n    'Got stuck on: the game.go options (the fade is the third argument), the pause menu item and setting shapes, and the headless draw path, which needs a canvas stub for road.draw (E.mkCanvas) and a renderer that answers every call. Guessed the Backdrop draw signature from the kit.',\n    'Most important thing built myself: the car model (acceleration calibrated to each car\\\\'s 0-100 rating, steering with the curve push, drift, slipstream, off-road), the traffic and lane logic, the driver brain, the run rules and the request rules.',\n    'Hardest part: a fork needs two roads drawn at once, and road.draw paints one road over the frame. Without a split-road renderer the fork is only signposted, and the road switches at the junction end.',\n    'Changed in the engine: nothing. Analog triggers are read from navigator.getGamepads() in game code, and the split-road renderer, the analog input and the other planned engine changes were not made.',\n    'One change I would make: a headless renderer or canvas stub in the engine, so draw code can run in tests without a browser.',\n  ],\n  promptFeedback: [\n    'Most liked: the plan is concrete. Every tuning number, every stage layout and every test suite is written down, which made the physics and the data quick to start.',\n    'Confusing: the plan was written for a different run (other model, other date, other folder names), and it asks for far more than one session can build (16 routes, 14 requests, 14 missions, 11 songs, Versus, the garden, AI Hub) with no cut list. TASK.md and the plan also disagree on the names, which made me choose TASK.md each time.',\n    'Hardest: getting the bot to hold the balance windows without a pad to tune by hand, and making a fork read as a fork without a split-road renderer.',\n    'Would change: give this run its own names and dates, state what to cut when time runs short, state the balance as a clock rule (the time per stage and the checkpoint bonus) rather than as bot windows, and say whether the bot uses the player\\\\'s physics.',\n  ],\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('about ok')\nEOF\nnode --check src/01-about.js && timeout 120 node build.mjs | tail -1 && python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(list(d.keys()), len(d['testingFeedback']), len(d['engineFeedback']), len(d['promptFeedback']))\"","description":"Fill feedback answers, rebuild, and validate the exit JSON"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01VmRcuryt9HQFBoSvhwKWSB":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-043153__xe1b7e1/work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153"}}}
