{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrJxKjA6SF42eJdBgPy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Status: the goal is not met\n\nThe game runs, but it does not meet the goal's \"done\" condition. TASK.md asks for every feature in full. This build is a partial vertical slice, and I'm stopping here rather than calling it done. The bot also cannot finish the routes on the default clock, so the core loop is not yet balanced.\n\n**Files**\n- Bundle: `work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153.html` (1.4 MB, loads from a file, title reached with no errors in a headless smoke test)\n- `work/exit-interview.json`: parses; every section is filled\n- Dev folder: `work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-…-20261104-043153/`. Source is in `src/`, the test command is `node tests/run.mjs` (106 checks, all passing), and `build.mjs` builds. Notes are in `NOTES.md`.\n\n**What works**\n- 15 stages built from layout data, with kit scenery. Forks are signposted and chosen by the car's side (or the bot's plan). Checkpoints extend the clock. Five goals, each with three moods (shown as text cards).\n- Car model: acceleration calibrated to each car's 0–100 rating, curve push held by steering, drift (brake tap, drift button, or down-up shift), slipstream and slingshot, off-road, crests, gusts.\n- Traffic with lane changes, overtakes, near misses and contacts. Love in Bloom with 10 request types, grades and moods.\n- Title, menu, garage (car, paint, passenger, radio), how to play, about and credits, results with records.\n- Attract mode after 10 s idle, Dev Mode from the pause menu (tuning sliders with reset, cheats, info), touch-only notice, PlayStation and Xbox button symbols.\n\n**What is missing or simplified**\n- **Balance:** on the default clock the bot fails most routes (time runs out around stages 2–3, with 7–14 crashes per route). I changed the start time to 100 s and checkpoint bonus to 71 s (plan: 75 s and 57 s, which also failed). The plan's balance windows are not met.\n- **Forks:** no split-road renderer (plan E1). The road switches to the chosen stage at the junction's end.\n- **Not built:** the Coast 2 Coast Tour and its 14 missions, the Garage Garden, Versus split-screen, time-trial ghosts and medals, and AI Hub online play. The AI Hub client is downloaded but not wired in.\n- **Requests:** bees, ribbons, bouquets and photo are missing.\n- **Endings:** text cards, not side-view vignettes. Passenger lines are 3–4 per reaction, not the full bank.\n- **Music and sound:** 5 radio songs plus 4 others; no engine loop; voices are syllable blips without formants.\n- **Art:** simple pixel shapes, not pre-rendered models. Passengers are head-and-shoulder portraits, not rigged characters.\n- **Dev Mode:** Tuning, Cheats and Info tabs only (no Warp, Audio or Save tabs).\n- **Checks not run:** no browser run, no screenshots, and touch emulation was not tested.\n\n**Decisions I made**\n- The title is the one from PLAN.md, which came from the plan's own RNG draw. I did not re-run a 50-title brainstorm myself.\n- PLAN.md's names and dates were stale (written for a different run), so I used TASK.md's names.\n- Gamepad triggers are read in game code, so the engine is unchanged.\n\n---\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 04:31:53\n- **Source:** OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast (SEGA / Sumo Digital, 2006), used as inspiration only\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade road racer with a passenger-request layer and a checkpoint route; third-person chase camera on a pseudo-3D road\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (MIT), JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio (the engine's chip synth)\n- **Art Direction:** engine pixel art at 480×270, drawn in code, dusk and sunrise palettes\n- **Animation:** engine sprite and px drawing (wheels, turbines, balloons, lights, bobbing passenger)\n- **Audio:** music and effects written in code on the engine synth; voices are syllable babble, no files\n- **Online:** none\n- **Testing:** headless suites through the engine (106 checks in `tests/run.mjs`); no browser run\n- **Research:** engine docs and the road kit read in full; the plan; public summaries of the source only\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about ten real defects. A stage transition dropped the carried distance, a goal re-entered its own stage, a fork read stage definitions as built stages, the bus was used before it was set, the drift exit was tied to the wrong value, the curve push was applied as a velocity increment, drag capped top speed near 170 km/h, the traffic spawner was time-based and over-filled the road, and lane changes oscillated.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** four would have broken a run outright: the stage skip, the goal re-entry, the fork crash and the bus crash on the first race. Each is now covered by a check.\n- **Most helpful test:** the full-route bot runs, which play all 16 forks to their goals with real distances, and exposed the stage-skip bug at once.\n- **Least helpful test:** the draw smoke test. It only shows that drawing code runs without an exception on a no-op renderer. It says nothing about what appears on screen.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the road module. `E.Road` with segments, curves, hills, `place()` and `project()` gave a working pseudo-3D road quickly, and the road kit was a complete reference game to read.\n- **Stuck or guessed:** the `game.go` options (the fade is the third argument), the pause-menu item and setting shapes, and the headless draw path. Road drawing needs a canvas stub (`E.mkCanvas`), and the renderer must answer every call. I guessed the Backdrop draw signature from the kit.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** the car model (calibrated to each car's rating, with steering, drift, slipstream and off-road), the traffic and lane logic, the driver brain, and the run and request rules.\n- **Hardest part:** a fork needs two roads drawn at once, and `road.draw` paints one road over the frame. Without a split-road renderer the fork is only signposted.\n- **Engine changes:** none. Analog triggers are read from `navigator.getGamepads()` in game code.\n- **Would change:** add a headless renderer or canvas stub, so draw code can run in tests without a browser.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan is concrete. Tuning numbers, stage layouts and test suites are all written down, which made the physics and the data quick to start.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was written for a different run (another model, date and folder names). It asks for far more than one session can build (16 routes, 14 requests, 14 missions, 11 songs, Versus, the garden, AI Hub) with no cut list. TASK.md and the plan also disagree on names.\n- **Hardest:** getting the bot to meet the balance windows without a pad to tune by hand, and making a fork read as a fork without a split-road renderer.\n- **Would change:** give each run its own names and dates, state what to cut when time runs short, express balance as a clock rule rather than bot windows, and say whether the bot uses the player's physics.\n\n**Next step:** I can keep going on balance (crash rate and clock), or cut scope to the Arcade and Love in Bloom loop and finish that properly. Tell me which you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":818,"cache_read_input_tokens":436559,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":818},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"e1513965-1d61-4f57-82e6-face9e3377e4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:00:35.936Z","request_id":"req_011CghrJwwu5xpSf7FpbTVgq"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The transcript's own final message says the goal is not met: 'The game runs, but it does not meet the goal's \"done\" condition. TASK.md asks for every feature in full. This build is a partial vertical slice.' It lists unbuilt features: the Coast 2 Coast Tour and its 14 missions, the Garage Garden, Versus split-screen, time-trial ghosts and medals, AI Hub online play (client downloaded but not wired in), missing request types (bees, ribbons, bouquets, photo), text-card endings instead of vignettes, and a Dev Mode without Warp, Audio or Save tabs. The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json do exist and parse, and the four required sections appear in the reply, but the feature-completeness requirement is not met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"e0061f48-04e7-44b5-94bf-361bda7abedc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:00:42.193Z","isSynthetic":true}
