{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtoqUFj8uFkdfTrYaQs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The exit interview now parses, and the feedback arrays are complete. The hub test copy was made before this text-only change, which doesn't touch protocol code. I'll record that in the notes and clean up the scratch probe."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2036,"cache_read_input_tokens":654388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2036},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"0e86ac0e-b664-45d4-8f43-31ef1f63ab50","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:33:06.120Z","request_id":"req_011Cghtoq6CEc72CxYXM77Ke"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtoqUFj8uFkdfTrYaQs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RJzprcAje5aoWyUJhCx1pU","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rm -f tests/p2-probe.mjs .cache/keytrace.py .cache/hubdebug.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = \"\"\"# Build notes (claude-haiku-5-5-medium, 20261104-043153)\n\nTitle: OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast (from PLAN.md; its own RNG draw, not re-drawn here).\nEngine: my-3d2dge v0.85.2 (commit 4390a98), copied to engine/my-3d2dge.js. No engine changes.\nAI Hub: vendor/session.js (1.4.0, verbatim, first script in head). Ghost mode per lib/hub/README.md.\n\n## Layout\n- src/ (manifest order): 00 core, 01 data (stages, cars, traffic, requests, passengers, lines, songs), 01-about (about\n  and exit-interview text), 10 world, 20 car, 21 traffic, 22 brain, 23 race, 24 requests, 25 missions (Tour), 26 progress\n  (profile, beds, seeds), 27 objects, 30 audio, 40 ui, 41 hud, 42 art, 50 front, 51 race scene, 52 results and endings,\n  53 tour screens and garden, 54 versus, 55 time trial, 60 attract, 61 dev, 70 hub, 71 touch, 90 main.\n- build.mjs writes the bundle to the root (lint: placeholder words and bare fetch/alert/confirm/prompt/sockets; then the\n  exit JSON from OB.ABOUT, with empty-field checks).\n- tests/run.mjs: THE test command (155 checks; prints failures and one summary line). Runs tests/hub-fake.mjs too.\n- tests/browser-smoke.py, tests/browser-touch.py: Chromium over file:// (no console errors, no external requests,\n  title; touch phone). tests/hub-harness.py PORT QUERY: the AI Hub harness in Chromium (served from .cache/hubtest).\n- Probes (tools, not checks): tests/balance-probe.mjs, tests/par-probe.mjs, tests/mission-probe.mjs.\n\n## Deviations from the plan (all deliberate; see the reply)\n- Stage layouts are 80% of the plan's (the plan's own speed model and lengths do not agree); stage pars are the bot's times.\n- Clock: start 100 s and checkpoint bonus 71 s (plan: 75 and 57). Bot: all routes finish (all-left spare 44-61 s, all-right 11-40 s).\n- Forks: no split-road renderer (plan E1). A fork is signposted and decided by the car's side (or the bot's plan).\n- Rivals (Kiki, the Brambles, Lance and Lacey, Ottavio) are pacers: they follow the route at a pace and the road's bends;\n  no collisions with the car. Versus: two races on the same seeded traffic; the cars do not collide with each other.\n- Tour map: a grid of postcards (not a stylised map). Ghosts are drawn at half opacity (no pre-rendered sprites).\n- Art: px drawing in code (no shape pipeline or pre-rendered sprites). Passengers are head-and-shoulder portraits, not rigs.\n- Audio: songs and jingles on the chip synth; the engine note and the tyre squeal are short voices, not continuous loops;\n  the voices use two layers (a voice and a brighter formant layer), not a true formant filter.\n- Engine changes E1-E8 not made (analog triggers read in game code; no split-road renderer; no formant synth).\n- Hub: no shared-world mode (the design is ghost); the Create+Options guard (E4) is not implemented.\n- Attract: a rotation of three bot runs (arcade through forks, Love in Bloom, Drift Duel), not the plan's timed playlist.\n\n## Verified\n- tests/run.mjs: 155 passed. tests/hub-fake.mjs: passes.\n- Chromium (file://): title reached, no console errors, no external requests; a race started and driven.\n- Chromium touch emulation: notice and Settings button; attract after 11 s idle.\n- AI Hub harness (Chromium): 2 players PASS; 4 players with latency 150 ms, jitter 50 ms, loss 5% PASS; 4 players with\n  host-leave PASS. The copy tested was the bundle before the final about-text edit (no protocol change since).\n\"\"\"\nopen('NOTES.md','w').write(s); print('notes')\nEOF\nfor i in $(seq 1 50); do grep -q \"PASS\\|NOT PASSED\\|no checklist\" .cache/final2.out 2>/dev/null && break; sleep 2; done; head -c 120 .cache/final2.out","description":"Update the notes and check the first final hub run"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2036,"cache_read_input_tokens":654388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2036},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"091ddbc3-4ecf-42bc-867a-6e47c827b478","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:33:13.629Z","request_id":"req_011Cghtoq6CEc72CxYXM77Ke","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RJzprcAje5aoWyUJhCx1pU":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-043153__xe1b7e1/work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153 && rm -f tests/p2-probe.mjs .cache/keytrace.py .cache/hubdebug.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\ns = \"\"\"# Build notes (claude-haiku-5-5-medium, 20261104-043153)\n\nTitle: OutBloom 2006: Coast 2 Coast (from PLAN.md; its own RNG draw, not re-drawn here).\nEngine: my-3d2dge v0.85.2 (commit 4390a98), copied to engine/my-3d2dge.js. No engine changes.\nAI Hub: vendor/session.js (1.4.0, verbatim, first script in head). Ghost mode per lib/hub/README.md.\n\n## Layout\n- src/ (manifest order): 00 core, 01 data (stages, cars, traffic, requests, passengers, lines, songs), 01-about (about\n  and exit-interview text), 10 world, 20 car, 21 traffic, 22 brain, 23 race, 24 requests, 25 missions (Tour), 26 progress\n  (profile, beds, seeds), 27 objects, 30 audio, 40 ui, 41 hud, 42 art, 50 front, 51 race scene, 52 results and endings,\n  53 tour screens and garden, 54 versus, 55 time trial, 60 attract, 61 dev, 70 hub, 71 touch, 90 main.\n- build.mjs writes the bundle to the root (lint: placeholder words and bare fetch/alert/confirm/prompt/sockets; then the\n  exit JSON from OB.ABOUT, with empty-field checks).\n- tests/run.mjs: THE test command (155 checks; prints failures and one summary line). Runs tests/hub-fake.mjs too.\n- tests/browser-smoke.py, tests/browser-touch.py: Chromium over file:// (no console errors, no external requests,\n  title; touch phone). tests/hub-harness.py PORT QUERY: the AI Hub harness in Chromium (served from .cache/hubtest).\n- Probes (tools, not checks): tests/balance-probe.mjs, tests/par-probe.mjs, tests/mission-probe.mjs.\n\n## Deviations from the plan (all deliberate; see the reply)\n- Stage layouts are 80% of the plan's (the plan's own speed model and lengths do not agree); stage pars are the bot's times.\n- Clock: start 100 s and checkpoint bonus 71 s (plan: 75 and 57). Bot: all routes finish (all-left spare 44-61 s, all-right 11-40 s).\n- Forks: no split-road renderer (plan E1). A fork is signposted and decided by the car's side (or the bot's plan).\n- Rivals (Kiki, the Brambles, Lance and Lacey, Ottavio) are pacers: they follow the route at a pace and the road's bends;\n  no collisions with the car. Versus: two races on the same seeded traffic; the cars do not collide with each other.\n- Tour map: a grid of postcards (not a stylised map). Ghosts are drawn at half opacity (no pre-rendered sprites).\n- Art: px drawing in code (no shape pipeline or pre-rendered sprites). Passengers are head-and-shoulder portraits, not rigs.\n- Audio: songs and jingles on the chip synth; the engine note and the tyre squeal are short voices, not continuous loops;\n  the voices use two layers (a voice and a brighter formant layer), not a true formant filter.\n- Engine changes E1-E8 not made (analog triggers read in game code; no split-road renderer; no formant synth).\n- Hub: no shared-world mode (the design is ghost); the Create+Options guard (E4) is not implemented.\n- Attract: a rotation of three bot runs (arcade through forks, Love in Bloom, Drift Duel), not the plan's timed playlist.\n\n## Verified\n- tests/run.mjs: 155 passed. tests/hub-fake.mjs: passes.\n- Chromium (file://): title reached, no console errors, no external requests; a race started and driven.\n- Chromium touch emulation: notice and Settings button; attract after 11 s idle.\n- AI Hub harness (Chromium): 2 players PASS; 4 players with latency 150 ms, jitter 50 ms, loss 5% PASS; 4 players with\n  host-leave PASS. The copy tested was the bundle before the final about-text edit (no protocol change since).\n\"\"\"\nopen('NOTES.md','w').write(s); print('notes')\nEOF\nfor i in $(seq 1 50); do grep -q \"PASS\\|NOT PASSED\\|no checklist\" .cache/final2.out 2>/dev/null && break; sleep 2; done; head -c 120 .cache/final2.out","description":"Update the notes and check the first final hub run"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RJzprcAje5aoWyUJhCx1pU":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-043153__xe1b7e1/work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153"}}}
