{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghudrufnrJT8w43x353D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine changes are in, the tests pass, and the race now uses the continuous voices. The last and hardest item is the fork renderer. The current road draws only the stage it is on, so beyond a junction it shows the same stage's start. I'll write a game-side renderer for the junction. It draws two branch surfaces with a widening gore between them, and it continues the next stage on each branch beyond the junction. Before the decision both branches are shown. After the decision only the chosen one is shown, and the car is kept on the branch, so the switch to the next stage is seamless."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1945,"cache_read_input_tokens":714907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1945},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"9f04b644-7079-4114-a1ff-a6c142eb2af9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:44:55.661Z","request_id":"req_011CghudrYqZoJ4YAXhgSDf1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghudrufnrJT8w43x353D","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F7ixj2n7c1beM5BpRDnc8T","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-043153__xe1b7e1/work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153/src/43-fork.js","content":"// The fork's renderer (plan E1, in game code): when a junction is in view the road splits. Two branch surfaces run out of\n// the junction, each centred on its own offset (the spread eases from 0 to 2.4 half-roads over the junction), with the\n// gore between them. Beyond the junction each branch carries on as its stage. Before the decision both are drawn; after\n// it, only the chosen one, and the car rides with it (its x is kept relative to the branch), so the switch to the next\n// stage at the junction's end does not move the picture. Painted far to near like the engine's road.\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, OB = window.OB || (window.OB = {});\nconst { px, clamp } = E;\nconst SPREAD = 2.4;\n\n/** the spread of the junction at a segment index of a stage: 0 before it, SPREAD after it, eased across it */\nfunction spreadAt(st, k) {\n  const j0 = Math.round(st.junction / OB.SEG), j1 = Math.round(st.len / OB.SEG);\n  if (k <= j0) return 0;\n  if (k >= j1) return SPREAD;\n  const u = (k - j0) / (j1 - j0);\n  return SPREAD * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\n}\nOB.spreadAt = spreadAt;\n\n/** the branch tracks at this moment: both before the decision, the chosen one after it */\nfunction tracksOf(race, st) {\n  if (!st.forkZ || !race.fork) return null;\n  const f = race.fork;\n  const [l, r] = OB.nextStages(st.def).map(d => OB.World.stage(d.id));\n  if (f.decided) return [{ side: f.side === 'L' ? -1 : 1, st: f.side === 'L' ? l : r }];\n  return [{ side: -1, st: l }, { side: 1, st: r }];\n}\n\n/** the depth bands of the view: each with its strips (the shared road, or one per branch) */\nfunction buildStrips(race, st, v, road) {\n  const segs = road.segs, N = segs.length, L = road.o.segment, drawN = road.o.draw;\n  const base = road.seg(v.z), baseIdx = base.i, pct = (v.z % L) / L;\n  const jIdx = Math.round(st.junction / L);\n  const tracks = tracksOf(race, st);\n  const out = [];\n  let x = -(base.curve * pct);                      // the shared bend, from the car's own segment\n  const shared = [];\n  for (let k = 0; k < drawN; k++) {\n    const idx = baseIdx + k;\n    if (idx < jIdx || !tracks) {\n      const s = segs[idx % N];\n      const wz = s.z + (s.i < baseIdx ? road.length : 0);\n      shared.push({ k, x, s, wz, off: 0, road, yoff: 0, mine: true });\n      x += 0; x += s.curve;\n      continue;\n    }\n    // a junction segment or beyond: each track carries its own bend from here on\n    const rows = [];\n    for (const t of tracks) {\n      const tr = t.tx === undefined ? { tx: x } : t;\n      if (idx < N) {\n        const s = segs[idx];\n        rows.push({ k, s, wz: s.z + (s.i < baseIdx ? road.length : 0), off: t.side * spreadAt(st, idx), x: tr.tx, road, yoff: 0 });\n      } else {\n        const ns = t.st.road.segs, nidx = idx - N;\n        if (nidx >= ns.length) continue;\n        const s = ns[nidx];\n        rows.push({ k, s, wz: s.z + (nidx * L), off: t.side * SPREAD, x: tr.tx, road: t.st.road, yoff: road.segs[N - 1].y1 });\n      }\n    }\n    for (const t of tracks) { const seg = idx < N ? segs[idx] : t.st.road.segs[idx - N]; if (seg) { t.tx = (t.tx === undefined ? x : t.tx) + seg.curve; } }\n    out.push(...rows);\n  }\n  return { shared, strips: out, tracks, baseIdx, pct, base, L };\n}\n\n/** a band of the road for one strip: its rumble, road and lanes (the grass is painted once per band before these) */\nfunction roadBand(g, vp, road, p1, p2, colors, alt, lanes) {\n  const quad = (x1, w1, x2, w2, c) => px.poly(g, [[x1 - w1, p1.y], [x1 + w1, p1.y], [x2 + w2, p2.y], [x2 - w2, p2.y]], c);\n  const k = Math.max(6, 2 * lanes);\n  quad(p1.x, p1.w * (1 + 1 / k), p2.x, p2.w * (1 + 1 / k), colors.rumble[alt]);\n  quad(p1.x, p1.w, p2.x, p2.w, colors.road[alt]);\n  if (!alt) for (let l = 1; l < lanes; l++) { const u = -1 + 2 * l / lanes; quad(p1.x + u * p1.w, p1.w / (16 * lanes), p2.x + u * p2.w, p2.w / (16 * lanes), colors.lane); }\n}\n\n/** draw the stage's view: the normal road when no junction is in view, else the split road */\nOB.drawStage = (r, race, v) => {\n  const st = race.stage, road = st.road;\n  const inView = !!st.forkZ && !!race.fork && !r.viewport && Math.floor(v.z / road.o.segment) + road.o.draw > Math.round(st.junction / road.o.segment) - 1;\n  if (!inView) return road.draw(r, v);\n  const o = road.o, W = r.W, H = r.H, t = race.stage && (OB.game.time || 0);\n  const { shared, strips, tracks, base, L } = buildStrips(race, st, v, road);\n  const C = { x: (v.x || 0) * o.width, y: (v.h === undefined ? o.height : v.h) + road.yAt(v.z), z: v.z, cx: W / 2, cy: H / 2, hw: W / 2, hh: H / 2, pct: (v.z % L) / L, bend: [] };\n  road._cam = C;\n  const fog = o.fog && E.hex(o.fog.color);\n  r.overlay(g => {\n    // the sky, as the road draws it, then the bands far to near\n    if (o.sky && o.sky.draw) o.sky.draw(Object.create(r, { ctx: { value: g }, bw: { value: W }, bh: { value: H }, W: { value: W }, H: { value: H }, ix: { value: v.turn || 0 }, iy: { value: 0 } }));\n    else E.px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, o.sky || '#6aa8e8');\n    // each depth: the shared road, and the strips of the branches, drawn far to near\n    const depths = new Map();\n    for (const row of shared) depths.set(row.k, [row]);\n    for (const row of strips) { if (!depths.has(row.k)) depths.set(row.k, []); depths.get(row.k).push(row); }\n    const ks = [...depths.keys()].sort((a, b) => b - a);\n    const cars = v.cars || [];\n    for (const k of ks) {\n      const rows = depths.get(k);\n      const prj = rows.map(row => {\n        const s = row.s, sd = row.road.o.colors;\n        const p1 = road._p(row.x * o.width + row.off * o.width, s.y0 + row.yoff, row.wz, C);\n        const p2 = road._p((row.x + s.curve * 0 + 0) * o.width + row.off * o.width, s.y1 + row.yoff, row.wz + L, C);\n        return { row, p1, p2, s, sd };\n      }).filter(q => q.p1 && q.p2 && q.p1.d > road.depth);\n      if (!prj.length) continue;\n      const q0 = prj[0];\n      const alt = Math.floor(q0.s.i / o.rumble) % 2;\n      const colors = q0.sd;\n      // the grass across the band, then the road surfaces of each branch\n      const fogF = fog ? 1 - Math.exp(-((k / o.draw) ** 2) * o.fog.density) : 0;\n      E.px.rect(g, 0, Math.min(q0.p1.y, q0.p2.y), W, Math.abs(q0.p1.y - q0.p2.y) + 1, colors.grass[alt]);\n      for (const q of prj) {\n        const cols = Object.assign({}, o.colors, q.s.colors ? q.s.colors : {}, q.sd);\n        roadBand(g, null, road, q.p1, q.p2, cols, Math.floor(q.s.i / o.rumble) % 2, q.row.road.o.lanes || o.lanes);\n      }\n      if (fogF > .01 && fog) { g.fillStyle = `rgba(${fog[0]},${fog[1]},${fog[2]},${fogF.toFixed(3)})`; g.fillRect(0, Math.min(q0.p1.y, q0.p2.y), W, Math.abs(q0.p1.y - q0.p2.y) + 1); E.px.reset(g); }\n      // the scenery of this depth, at its track's centre\n      for (const q of prj) {\n        const things = q.s.things || [];\n        g.globalAlpha = 1;\n        for (const th of things) road._thing(g, th.what, q.p1.x + q.p1.scale * th.offset * o.width, q.p1.y, q.p1.scale, th.scale, t);\n      }\n      for (const c of cars) {\n        if (c.z < v.z - L || c.z > v.z + L) continue;\n        const seg = road.seg(c.z), q = prj.find(qq => qq.s === seg) || prj[0];\n        if (!q) continue;\n        const u = (((c.z - q.wz) % road.length + road.length) % road.length) / L;\n        road._thing(g, c, q.p1.x + (q.p2.x - q.p1.x) * u + q.p1.scale * c.x * o.width, q.p1.y + (q.p2.y - q.p1.y) * u, q.p1.scale, 8, t);\n      }\n    }\n    E.px.reset(g);\n  });\n  return road;\n};\n})();\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1945,"cache_read_input_tokens":714907,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1945},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"5b4757e9-d47e-464f-b6b2-503cf7ad257d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:45:09.011Z","request_id":"req_011CghudrYqZoJ4YAXhgSDf1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01F7ixj2n7c1beM5BpRDnc8T":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-043153__xe1b7e1/work/OutBloom2006Coast2Coast-OutRun2006Coast2Coast-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-043153/src/43-fork.js","content":"// The fork's renderer (plan E1, in game code): when a junction is in view the road splits. Two branch surfaces run out of\n// the junction, each centred on its own offset (the spread eases from 0 to 2.4 half-roads over the junction), with the\n// gore between them. Beyond the junction each branch carries on as its stage. Before the decision both are drawn; after\n// it, only the chosen one, and the car rides with it (its x is kept relative to the branch), so the switch to the next\n// stage at the junction's end does not move the picture. Painted far to near like the engine's road.\n(() => {\n'use strict';\nconst E = My3D2dge, OB = window.OB || (window.OB = {});\nconst { px, clamp } = E;\nconst SPREAD = 2.4;\n\n/** the spread of the junction at a segment index of a stage: 0 before it, SPREAD after it, eased across it */\nfunction spreadAt(st, k) {\n  const j0 = Math.round(st.junction / OB.SEG), j1 = Math.round(st.len / OB.SEG);\n  if (k <= j0) return 0;\n  if (k >= j1) return SPREAD;\n  const u = (k - j0) / (j1 - j0);\n  return SPREAD * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\n}\nOB.spreadAt = spreadAt;\n\n/** the branch tracks at this moment: both before the decision, the chosen one after it */\nfunction tracksOf(race, st) {\n  if (!st.forkZ || !race.fork) return null;\n  const f = race.fork;\n  const [l, r] = OB.nextStages(st.def).map(d => OB.World.stage(d.id));\n  if (f.decided) return [{ side: f.side === 'L' ? -1 : 1, st: f.side === 'L' ? l : r }];\n  return [{ side: -1, st: l }, { side: 1, st: r }];\n}\n\n/** the depth bands of the view: each with its strips (the shared road, or one per branch) */\nfunction buildStrips(race, st, v, road) {\n  const segs = road.segs, N = segs.length, L = road.o.segment, drawN = road.o.draw;\n  const base = road.seg(v.z), baseIdx = base.i, pct = (v.z % L) / L;\n  const jIdx = Math.round(st.junction / L);\n  const tracks = tracksOf(race, st);\n  const out = [];\n  let x = -(base.curve * pct);                      // the shared bend, from the car's own segment\n  const shared = [];\n  for (let k = 0; k < drawN; k++) {\n    const idx = baseIdx + k;\n    if (idx < jIdx || !tracks) {\n      const s = segs[idx % N];\n      const wz = s.z + (s.i < baseIdx ? road.length : 0);\n      shared.push({ k, x, s, wz, off: 0, road, yoff: 0, mine: true });\n      x += 0; x += s.curve;\n      continue;\n    }\n    // a junction segment or beyond: each track carries its own bend from here on\n    const rows = [];\n    for (const t of tracks) {\n      const tr = t.tx === undefined ? { tx: x } : t;\n      if (idx < N) {\n        const s = segs[idx];\n        rows.push({ k, s, wz: s.z + (s.i < baseIdx ? road.length : 0), off: t.side * spreadAt(st, idx), x: tr.tx, road, yoff: 0 });\n      } else {\n        const ns = t.st.road.segs, nidx = idx - N;\n        if (nidx >= ns.length) continue;\n        const s = ns[nidx];\n        rows.push({ k, s, wz: s.z + (nidx * L), off: t.side * SPREAD, x: tr.tx, road: t.st.road, yoff: road.segs[N - 1].y1 });\n      }\n    }\n    for (const t of tracks) { const seg = idx < N ? segs[idx] : t.st.road.segs[idx - N]; if (seg) { t.tx = (t.tx === undefined ? x : t.tx) + seg.curve; } }\n    out.push(...rows);\n  }\n  return { shared, strips: out, tracks, baseIdx, pct, base, L };\n}\n\n/** a band of the road for one strip: its rumble, road and lanes (the grass is painted once per band before these) */\nfunction roadBand(g, vp, road, p1, p2, colors, alt, lanes) {\n  const quad = (x1, w1, x2, w2, c) => px.poly(g, [[x1 - w1, p1.y], [x1 + w1, p1.y], [x2 + w2, p2.y], [x2 - w2, p2.y]], c);\n  const k = Math.max(6, 2 * lanes);\n  quad(p1.x, p1.w * (1 + 1 / k), p2.x, p2.w * (1 + 1 / k), colors.rumble[alt]);\n  quad(p1.x, p1.w, p2.x, p2.w, colors.road[alt]);\n  if (!alt) for (let l = 1; l < lanes; l++) { const u = -1 + 2 * l / lanes; quad(p1.x + u * p1.w, p1.w / (16 * lanes), p2.x + u * p2.w, p2.w / (16 * lanes), colors.lane); }\n}\n\n/** draw the stage's view: the normal road when no junction is in view, else the split road */\nOB.drawStage = (r, race, v) => {\n  const st = race.stage, road = st.road;\n  const inView = !!st.forkZ && !!race.fork && !r.viewport && Math.floor(v.z / road.o.segment) + road.o.draw > Math.round(st.junction / road.o.segment) - 1;\n  if (!inView) return road.draw(r, v);\n  const o = road.o, W = r.W, H = r.H, t = race.stage && (OB.game.time || 0);\n  const { shared, strips, tracks, base, L } = buildStrips(race, st, v, road);\n  const C = { x: (v.x || 0) * o.width, y: (v.h === undefined ? o.height : v.h) + road.yAt(v.z), z: v.z, cx: W / 2, cy: H / 2, hw: W / 2, hh: H / 2, pct: (v.z % L) / L, bend: [] };\n  road._cam = C;\n  const fog = o.fog && E.hex(o.fog.color);\n  r.overlay(g => {\n    // the sky, as the road draws it, then the bands far to near\n    if (o.sky && o.sky.draw) o.sky.draw(Object.create(r, { ctx: { value: g }, bw: { value: W }, bh: { value: H }, W: { value: W }, H: { value: H }, ix: { value: v.turn || 0 }, iy: { value: 0 } }));\n    else E.px.rect(g, 0, 0, W, H, o.sky || '#6aa8e8');\n    // each depth: the shared road, and the strips of the branches, drawn far to near\n    const depths = new Map();\n    for (const row of shared) depths.set(row.k, [row]);\n    for (const row of strips) { if (!depths.has(row.k)) depths.set(row.k, []); depths.get(row.k).push(row); }\n    const ks = [...depths.keys()].sort((a, b) => b - a);\n    const cars = v.cars || [];\n    for (const k of ks) {\n      const rows = depths.get(k);\n      const prj = rows.map(row => {\n        const s = row.s, sd = row.road.o.colors;\n        const p1 = road._p(row.x * o.width + row.off * o.width, s.y0 + row.yoff, row.wz, C);\n        const p2 = road._p((row.x + s.curve * 0 + 0) * o.width + row.off * o.width, s.y1 + row.yoff, row.wz + L, C);\n        return { row, p1, p2, s, sd };\n      }).filter(q => q.p1 && q.p2 && q.p1.d > road.depth);\n      if (!prj.length) continue;\n      const q0 = prj[0];\n      const alt = Math.floor(q0.s.i / o.rumble) % 2;\n      const colors = q0.sd;\n      // the grass across the band, then the road surfaces of each branch\n      const fogF = fog ? 1 - Math.exp(-((k / o.draw) ** 2) * o.fog.density) : 0;\n      E.px.rect(g, 0, Math.min(q0.p1.y, q0.p2.y), W, Math.abs(q0.p1.y - q0.p2.y) + 1, colors.grass[alt]);\n      for (const q of prj) {\n        const cols = Object.assign({}, o.colors, q.s.colors ? q.s.colors : {}, q.sd);\n        roadBand(g, null, road, q.p1, q.p2, cols, Math.floor(q.s.i / o.rumble) % 2, q.row.road.o.lanes || o.lanes);\n      }\n      if (fogF > .01 && fog) { g.fillStyle = `rgba(${fog[0]},${fog[1]},${fog[2]},${fogF.toFixed(3)})`; g.fillRect(0, Math.min(q0.p1.y, q0.p2.y), W, Math.abs(q0.p1.y - q0.p2.y) + 1); E.px.reset(g); }\n      // the scenery of this depth, at its track's centre\n      for (const q of prj) {\n        const things = q.s.things || [];\n        g.globalAlpha = 1;\n        for (const th of things) road._thing(g, th.what, q.p1.x + q.p1.scale * th.offset * o.width, q.p1.y, q.p1.scale, th.scale, t);\n      }\n      for (const c of cars) {\n        if (c.z < v.z - L || c.z > v.z + L) continue;\n        const seg = road.seg(c.z), q = prj.find(qq => qq.s === seg) || prj[0];\n        if (!q) continue;\n        const u = (((c.z - q.wz) % road.length + road.length) % road.length) / L;\n        road._thing(g, c, q.p1.x + (q.p2.x - q.p1.x) * u + q.p1.scale * c.x * o.width, q.p1.y + (q.p2.y - q.p1.y) * u, q.p1.scale, 8, t);\n      }\n    }\n    E.px.reset(g);\n  });\n  return road;\n};\n})();\n"}}}
