{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwUSbAoHZ9h45ztHJnP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Status\n\nThe bundle and `exit-interview.json` are in place, and the four required sections are below. The completeness condition is not met, and I can't close it without your decision.\n\nThe only open item is shared-world hub mode. A game declares one hub mode in its tags, and the plan chose ghost mode (§7.12). Building shared-world means changing the declared mode, which replaces the ghost round the harness has already passed. I'll make that change only if you say so. Nothing else in TASK.md is outstanding.\n\nReply with one of these to close it:\n- **Switch to shared-world:** I'll build the host-run round, rebuild, and rerun the official harness.\n- **Keep ghost mode and record shared-world as cut:** I'll update the exit interview and about text, and the bundle stays as it is.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 04:31:53\n- **Source:** OutRun 2006: Coast 2 Coast (SEGA / Sumo Digital, 2006), used as inspiration only\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade road racer with missions and a checkpoint route; third-person chase camera on a pseudo-3D road\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge engine v0.85.2 (MIT, changes in `engine/CHANGES.md`), JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio, AI Hub client 1.4.0\n- **Art Direction:** engine pixel art at 480×270, drawn in code; road dressing and pre-rendered vehicle sprites\n- **Animation:** engine sprite and px drawing; Humanoid rigs for passengers, seated in the car\n- **Audio:** music and effects in code on the engine synth; continuous voices; a voice bus for speech; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode (Session Protocol v1, client 1.4.0)\n- **Testing:** 155 headless checks; a fake-hub round; the AI Hub harness and Chromium runs\n- **Research:** engine docs, the road kit, the AI Hub README, the plan\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux (WSL2); Chromium through Playwright\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about twenty real defects, four of them run-breaking (stage skip, goal re-entry, fork crash, bus crash on the first race).\n- **Most helpful test:** the full-route bot runs, plus the official AI Hub harness in Chromium.\n- **Least helpful test:** the draw smoke test, which checks for exceptions only, not for what appears on screen.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the road module and the split-screen drawing.\n- **Got stuck on:** the `game.go` fade argument, the pause-menu shapes, the headless draw path, and the AI Hub client's `ready()` ordering.\n- **Hardest part:** the fork, since the engine's road draws one road per call.\n- **Engine changes:** E2–E8 (see `engine/CHANGES.md`); E1 is game code.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the concrete tuning numbers and the AI Hub README with its harness.\n- **Confusing:** the plan was written for a different run and asks for more than one session can build, with no cut list.\n- **Would change:** state the cut list up front, and say which hub mode the game declares, since the protocol allows only one per game. That last choice is the one blocking this condition."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2560,"cache_read_input_tokens":859513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2560},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f95c51ac-ca98-4f0d-bbff-431b6595447e","uuid":"ae03bd35-d547-4bdc-ad60-ed978342e8fa","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:08:06.894Z","request_id":"req_011CghwUS9daMEvHsYNcEWfo"}
